00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:29.590
And I will say it an example of kind of a
more extreme version.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:30.590
Yeah.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:40.600
So, for example, people who are already easily
sensitized are disgusted by insects and afraid

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:48.440
of, you know, people some of us are totally
freaked out by insects or spiders.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:53.560
Some of us, you know, not so much.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:12:02.160
There's a condition called Delusions of Infestation
that I have have worked on for for several

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.950
years now.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.750
And it's it's really upsetting.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:15.949
It's where people develop the idea that insects
or other small creatures have and have literally

00:12:15.949 --> 00:12:17.580
infested their bodies.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.580
Right.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.550
And and it often starts with something real.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:25.350
Like an itch could be as simple as a skin
condition that's causing an itch.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:33.380
But because people some people are already
kind of worried about insects or just sort

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:42.949
of more prone to to feel disgust about insects,
if they happen to see an insect in the environment,

00:12:42.949 --> 00:12:46.530
they may make the connection that, oh, I think
